plex is neutral, so the metal is Cr(III), d³; d³ + 12 e from the ligands = 15 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Oxidation state","a":"What is the oxidation state of Cr?","o":[{"x":"+3"},{"x":"+4"},{"x":"+2"},{"x":"+1"}],"t":"Tris(acetylacetonato)chromium","f":"Cr(acac)₃","fig":{"m":2449},"ex":"Covalent count: Cr (group 6) 6 e; 3 × acac (LX) 9 e: 15 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry a charge of −3 in all and the complex is neutral, so the metal is Cr(III), d³; d³ + 12 e from the ligands = 15 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"dⁿ count","a":"What is the dⁿ count of Cr?","o":[{"x":"d³"},{"x":"d²"},{"x":"d⁴"},{"x":"d⁵"}],"t":"Tris(acetylacetonato)chromium","f":"Cr(acac)₃","fig":{"m":2449},"ex":"Covalent count: Cr (group 6) 6 e; 3 × acac (LX) 9 e: 15 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry a charge of −3 in all and the complex is neutral, so the metal is Cr(III), d³; d³ + 12 e from the ligands = 15 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Geometry","a":"What shape is it?","o":[{"x":"Octahedral"},{"x":"Trigonal prismatic"},{"x":"Trigonal bipyramidal"},{"x":"Trigonal planar"}],"t":"Tris(acetylacetonato)chromium","f":"Cr(acac)₃","fig":{"m":2449},"ex":"Octahedral. Covalent count: Cr (group 6) 6 e; 3 × acac (LX) 9 e: 15 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry a charge of −3 in all and the complex is neutral, so the metal is Cr(III), d³; d³ + 12 e from the ligands = 15 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Electron count","a":"How many valence electrons does Ru have?","o":[{"x":"18 e"},{"x":"17 e"},{"x":"19 e"},{"x":"20 e"}],"t":"Pentaammine(dinitrogen)ruthenium(II)","f":"[Ru(NH₃)₅(N₂)]²⁺","fig":{"m":2450},"ex":"Covalent count: Ru (group 8) 8 e; 1 × N₂ (L) 2 e; 5 × NH₃ (L) 10 e; the 2+ charge removes 2 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex has a 2+ charge, so the metal is Ru(II), d⁶; d⁶ + 12 e from the ligands = 18 e. The first dinitrogen complex (1965).","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Oxidation state","a":"What is the oxidation state of Ru?","o":[{"x":"+2"},{"x":"+3"},{"x":"+1"},{"x":"0"}],"t":"Pentaammine(dinitrogen)ruthenium(II)","f":"[Ru(NH₃)₅(N₂)]²⁺","fig":{"m":2450},"ex":"Covalent count: Ru (group 8) 8 e; 1 × N₂ (L) 2 e; 5 × NH₃ (L) 10 e; the 2+ charge removes 2 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex has a 2+ charge, so the metal is Ru(II), d⁶; d⁶ + 12 e from the ligands = 18 e. The first dinitrogen complex (1965).","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"dⁿ count","a":"What is the dⁿ count of Ru?","o":[{"x":"d⁶"},{"x":"d⁷"},{"x":"d⁵"},{"x":"d⁴"}],"t":"Pentaammine(dinitrogen)ruthenium(II)","f":"[Ru(NH₃)₅(N₂)]²⁺","fig":{"m":2450},"ex":"Covalent count: Ru (group 8) 8 e; 1 × N₂ (L) 2 e; 5 × NH₃ (L) 10 e; the 2+ charge removes 2 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex has a 2+ charge, so the metal is Ru(II), d⁶; d⁶ + 12 e from the ligands = 18 e. The first dinitrogen complex (1965).","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Geometry","a":"What shape is it?","o":[{"x":"Octahedral"},{"x":"Trigonal prismatic"},{"x":"Trigonal bipyramidal"},{"x":"Trigonal planar"}],"t":"Pentaammine(dinitrogen)ruthenium(II)","f":"[Ru(NH₃)₅(N₂)]²⁺","fig":{"m":2450},"ex":"Octahedral. Covalent count: Ru (group 8) 8 e; 1 × N₂ (L) 2 e; 5 × NH₃ (L) 10 e; the 2+ charge removes 2 e: 18 e. I